														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3714643">
									

<p>This SCP has a really strong 'Cold War' vibe to it that I can't put my finger on; also, the idea of an anomaly that centers on a murder mystery that <em>must not be solved</em> is very cool.</p>
<p>I like this as it is, although I was also hoping for something in the fragmented records that indicated multiple narratives that are all simultaneously true (IE, O5-9 was killed by several people, and several methods, at several different times), with each O5 member being made aware of a different murder, and responsible for ensuring the evidence for this particular murder remains contained/does not interact with any evidence from the other variants (else we cause the emergence of destructive causal contradictions).</p>
<p>That being said, this took a much more low-key approach to the idea &#8212; one which I think also works really well.</p>

