<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>O5-8 probably did it, as the &quot;this document must be destroyed&quot; was in O5-1's fragment of the description, but O5-8 was the one to delete it. O5-8 may have been trying to cover their tracks by fabricating TRAILHEAD so as to not give anyone enough conclusive information to point the murder back to him, then deleting it all as a supposed end of the world-preventing measure.</p>
<p>The big hole in this theory is the segment stating that a list of 15 suspects was compiled, but then again all of the agencies that compiled that list were not Foundation insiders. Said list probably did not include O5 Command, as I find it would be a major breach of security to let any of those agencies know enough about O5 to compile a list including any of them.</p>
<p>I feel like there was a massive missed potential in a &quot;seven ate nine&quot; joke with this article.</p>
