			<div class="content" id="post-content-4334752">
									

<p>+1</p>
<p>Here's my headcanon:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>&quot;The fellow O5 murdered a colleague&quot; ties up a lot of things except for all of the wonkiness that happened that day (The sight of a daylight comment, the undecipherable language bit, etc.) and I just think it's too <em>clean</em> and too <em>mundane</em> to say all of the evidence was fabricated by a rival O5, or even that an O5 used anomalous means to create the wonkiness as red herrings.</p>
<p>My headcanon is that TRAILHEAD <em>did</em> work, but not in the intended way. The specific language is that &quot;O5-9 would only die as the result of a naturally-occurring, age-related illness.&quot; We're also told that it &quot;ensured that O5-9 would meet a specific demise involving a gunshot(s) to the head.&quot; I think both are simultaneously <em>true</em> statements.</p>
<p>Maybe it was a mistake, and O5-9 didn't realize the second effect. Maybe he did, and he was attempting quantum immortality by ensuring two utterly <strong>incompatible</strong> future deaths. Either way, he was so <em>sure</em> that his little plan worked, he let his guard down. He had fewer security guards, fewer countermeasures, and no other anomalous protections. A would be-assassin actually made it into his dining room. But just as the assassin is about to pull the trigger, the universe goes wonky. Time speeds up. Local broadcast stations start playing messages from dozens of years in the future, in a yet-to-be-created language. Halley's Comet, not scheduled to arrive for another 75 years, appears in the sky. Individuals vanish and others skip ahead weeks or months into the future.</p>
<p>O5-9 is aged a lifetime in a few moments just as his assassin pulls the trigger. O5-9 dies of natural coronary failure, just as the bullets strike him. Both deaths happen simultaneously.</p>
</div>
